eep the computation tied to the spatial field.","weight":0.86,"seconds":10,"archetype":"equation-walk","params":{"eyebrow":"Carrier definition","headline":"The carrier is encoded first, then windowed","equationId":"eq-carrier","terms":[{"tex":"\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}","label":"low-resolution input","tone":"a"},{"tex":"\\mathcal{E}","label":"encoder that builds features","tone":"b"},{"tex":"\\mathbf{F}","label":"dense carrier field","tone":"c"},{"tex":"\\mathcal{W}","label":"windowing over the carrier","tone":"d"}]}},{"id":"b06-architecture","intent":"The viewer understands that ThinkSR runs end to end through encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, and decoder.","inside":null,"claim":"ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.","evidence":[{"kind":"figure","id":"fig-arch"}],"narration":"The end-to-end path starts by encoding the low-resolution image. The encoded field is split into windows. Shared DQ-CTM ticks process those windows. The decoder turns the processed field into the reconstruction.","weight":0.94,"seconds":11,"archetype":"pipeline","params":{"eyebrow":"End to end","headline":"ThinkSR flows from encoder to windows to shared ticks to decoder","stages":[{"label":"Encoder","note":"Low-resolution image to features","tone":"a"},{"label":"Windows","note":"Feature field is partitioned","tone":"b"},{"label":"Shared DQ-CTM ticks","note":"Repeated compact updates","tone":"c"},{"label":"Decoder","note":"Output reconstruction","tone":"d"}],"loop":null,"note":"The stages match the end-to-end diagram."}},{"id":"b07-windows","intent":"The viewer understands that windowing is the spatial structure inside the ThinkSR path.","inside":{"beat":"b06-architecture","element":"stage1"},"claim":"ThinkSR end to end: encoder, windows, shared DQ-CTM ticks, decoder.","evidence":[{"kind":"figure","id":"fig-arch"},{"kind":"equation","id":"eq-carrier"}],"narration":"Windowing gives the dense carrier a local structure. Each lit region is part of the same carrier. The partition is the bridge from field data into window-level processing.","weight":0.68,"seconds":8,"archetype":"grid","params":{"eyebrow":"Windows","headline":"The carrier is partitioned into window inputs","cols":4,"rows":3,"regions":[{"x":0,"y":0,"w":2,"h":2,"label":"Window input","tone":"a"},{"x":2,"y":0,"w":2,"h":2,"label":"Window input","tone":"b"},{"x":0,"y":2,"w":2,"h":1,"label":"Window input","tone":"c"}],"note":"The equation names this operation as windowing over the carrier."}},{"id":"b08-progress","intent":"The viewer understands that the reconstruction is shown across ticks from T=0 through T=4, compared with bicubic and ground truth.","inside":null,"claim":"Reconstruction at T=0 through T=4 against bicubic and ground truth.","evidence":[{"kind":"figure","id":"fig-progress"}],"narration":"The reconstruction is tracked across successive ticks. The starting point is compared with bicubic. Later ticks show the same crop as the process continues. Ground truth anchors the comparison.","weight":0.8,"seconds":10,"archetype":"annotated-figure","params":{"eyebrow":"Reconstruction progress","headline":"Reconstruction is shown from T=0 through T=4","figureId":"fig-progress","crop":null,"notes":[{"x":0.18,"y":0.25,"text":"Bicubic reference","tone":"a"},{"x":0.36,"y":0.25,"text":"T=0 reconstruction","tone":"b"},{"x":0.6,"y":0.25,"text":"Ticks T=1 to T=4","tone":"c"},{"x":0.84,"y":0.25,"text":"Ground truth","tone":"d"}]}},{"id":"b09-error","intent":"The viewer understands that the error maps use the same crops and one shared colour scale.","inside":null,"claim":"Absolute-error maps on the same crops, one shared colour scale.","evidence":[{"kind":"figure","id":"fig-error"}],"narration":"The error maps compare absolute error on the same crops. A shared colour scale keeps the maps comparable. That makes differences in error intensity meaningful across methods.","weight":0.76,"seconds":8,"archetype":"annotated-figure","params":{"eyebrow":"Error maps","headline":"Absolute error is compared on one shared colour scale","figureId":"fig-error","crop":null,"notes":[{"x":0.2,"y":0.35,"text":"Same crop basis","tone":"a"},{"x":0.52,"y":0.35,"text":"Absolute-error maps","tone":"b"},{"x":0.84,"y":0.35,"text":"Shared colour scale","tone":"c"}]}},{"id":"b10-results-table","intent":"The viewer understands that DQ-CTM-SR is competitive with CNN baselines but trails the recent lightweight transformer CATANet.","inside":null,"claim":"Competitive with CNN baselines; behind recent lightweight transformers.","evidence":[{"kind":"section","id":"sec3"},{"kind":"table","id":"tbl-bench"}],"narration":"The benchmark reports parameters and average score together. DQ-CTM-SR is close to the CNN baselines in average score. CATANet has the highest reported average. DQ-CTM-SR uses more parameters than the listed lightweight transformer.","weight":0.93,"seconds":11,"archetype":"data-table","params":{"eyebrow":"Results","headline":"DQ-CTM-SR is competitive with CNNs but behind CATANet","tableId":"tbl-bench","highlight":[{"row":"IMDN","tone":"a"},{"row":"RFDN","tone":"a"},{"row":"CATANet","tone":"c"},{"row":"DQ-CTM-SR","tone":"b"}],"note":"Average is over five benchmarks for x4 lightweight super-resolution."}},{"id":"b11-params","intent":"The viewer understands that DQ-CTM-SR has more parameters than IMDN, RFDN, and CATANet in the reported table, but fewer than CARN.","inside":null,"claim":"DQ-CTM-SR | 1.129M | 28.983","evidence":[{"kind":"table","id":"tbl-bench"}],"narration":"Parameter count shows a different tradeoff than score. CARN is the largest listed model. DQ-CTM-SR is smaller than CARN. It is larger than IMDN, RFDN, and CATANet.","weight":0.58,"seconds":9,"archetype":"bar-compare","params":{"eyebrow":"Model size","headline":"DQ-CTM-SR sits between CARN and smaller baselines in size","unit":"M parameters","bars":[{"label":"CARN","value":1.592,"tone":"a"},{"label":"DQ-CTM-SR","value":1.129,"tone":"b"},{"label":"IMDN","value":0.715,"tone":"c"},{"label":"RFDN","value":0.55,"tone":"c"},{"label":"CATANet","value":0.535,"tone":"d"}],"note":"Values are the reported parameter counts."}},{"id":"b12-score","intent":"The viewer understands that DQ-CTM-SR's average score is near CARN, IMDN, and RFDN, while CATANet is higher.","inside":null,"claim":"DQ-CTM-SR | 1.129M | 28.983","evidence":[{"kind":"table","id":"tbl-bench"},{"kind":"section","id":"sec3"}],"narration":"Average score is tightly grouped for the CNN baselines and DQ-CTM-SR. RFDN reports a slightly higher average than DQ-CTM-SR. CATANet is the clear leader in this table. That is the stated gap to recent lightweight transformers.","weight":0.82,"seconds":10,"archetype":"bar-compare","params":{"eyebrow":"Average score","headline":"DQ-CTM-SR is close to CNN baselines and below CATANet","unit":"average score","bars":[{"label":"CATANet","value":29.482,"tone":"d"},{"label":"RFDN","value":29.022,"tone":"c"},{"label":"DQ-CTM-SR","value":28.983,"tone":"b"},{"label":"CARN","value":28.97,"tone":"a"},{"label":"IMDN","value":28.968,"tone":"a"}],"note":"Average is reported over five benchmarks."}}]}
